# Aster v2 — Attribution

This project incorporates the following third-party components.

## PyKEP — ESA's scientific library for spacecraft trajectory analysis

- Repository: https://github.com/esa/pykep
- Component used: Lambert problem solver (lambert_problem.cpp and supporting headers)
- Algorithm: Izzo 2014, "Revisiting Lambert's Problem" (arXiv:1403.2705)
- Version pinned: v3.0.0 (commit e01667f61be6c9dcc24db813e57d760ffd7f7810)
- License: Mozilla Public License version 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
- SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
- Usage: The Lambert solver C++ source is vendored at src/v2/vendor/pykep-lambert/, compiled to WebAssembly, and used for Earth-departure screening in Slice 10 of Aster v2's trajectory layer.

The PyKEP project copyright is held by its upstream contributors. The vendored
files preserve their original MPL-2.0 copyright headers verbatim. Modifications
to vendored files are documented in src/v2/vendor/pykep-lambert/UPSTREAM.md.

MPL-2.0 full text: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/

## Tycho-2 star catalog

- Source: VizieR, ESO
- Component used: V_T <= 8.1 all-sky subset (40,000 stars) for visualization background
- Citation: Hog, E. et al. 2000, "The Tycho-2 Catalogue of the 2.5 Million Brightest Stars," Astronomy & Astrophysics 355, L27
- Distribution: This subset is included in the Aster v2 repository at tests/fixtures/v2/star-catalog-tycho2-mag75.bin

## NEA catalog data

- Source: NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory, Small-Body Database (SBDB)
- URL: https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/sbdb_query.api
- Usage: NEA orbital elements ingested for the 41,906-body catalog. See Slice 9 founding doc for full ingestion methodology.

## Solar system body ephemerides

- Source: NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory, Horizons System
- URL: https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/
- Component used: Tabulated state vectors (position, velocity) for Sun, Mercury, Venus, Earth, Moon, Mars across 2026-2040 at daily cadence
- Distribution: tests/fixtures/v2/horizons-inner-solar-system-2026-2040.json
- Generator: tools/slice10-research/extend-horizons-fixture.mjs
